{
  "requirement": "Under {cite}`requirements.cli.skill_structure`, the `habeas-requirements` skill MUST be the home of drafting, reviewing, and agreeing requirements, the requirement review criteria, the procedure for choosing references, and the criteria the assessment applies to code and tests.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject says the `habeas-requirements` skill MUST be the home of six topics: drafting, reviewing and agreeing requirements; the requirement review criteria; the procedure for choosing references; and the criteria the assessment applies to code and tests. The parent text adds that each topic is stated in full in exactly one skill.\n\nThe marked test is `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_is_home_of_drafting_review_references_and_criteria]`. It covers each obligation as follows:\n- **Drafting, reviewing and agreeing:** `workflow_steps(\"habeas-requirements\")` must contain a step with \"Draft. Write drafts\", one with \"Review. Sort the new and changed requirements\", and one with \"**Gate:**\". The assertion `.any(...)` over the parsed numbered Workflow steps enforces each.\n- **Choosing references:** the `## Choosing references` section of `SKILL.md`, extracted by `section`, must contain \"A *root* is\".\n- **Criteria applied to code and tests:** the `## What the review checks` section must contain \"obligations, boundaries, and failure cases no test runs and asserts\" and \"The supervising agent must still check that the code fulfills each applicable requirement\". Together these cover the test-side and code-side criteria.\n- **Requirement review criteria:** the `## Criteria` section of `references/review-prompt.md`, which belongs to the skill, must contain \"**Compound:**\", \"**Checkable:**\" and \"**One reading:**\".\n- **Exactly one home:** `assert_home(\"habeas-requirements\")` first asserts that the skill (`SKILL.md` plus its references) contains every marker in `home_markers`. The markers cover drafting, the per-group subagent review, the gate, the root definition, the \"What the review checks\" heading, the \"Requirement group review\" prompt, and the Compound criterion. It then asserts that none of the other four skills in `SKILLS` contains any of those markers. A violation, such as another skill restating these topics or the requirements skill lacking them, would fail the test.\n\nThe helpers (`skill_md`, `skill_file`, `section`, `workflow_steps`, `assert_text`, `assert_home`, `bundled_skill`) are reached from the marked test and need no references of their own. They make real content assertions. `bundled_skills_are_five_skill_directories_each_home_to_its_topics`, marked for the parent requirement, separately covers skill structure and uniqueness across the whole set.\n\nNo obligation in the subject lacks a scenario and an assertion. The markers are phrase-based, which is the natural way to test where prose is stated. I found no gap and no acknowledgments apply.",
  "references": "f159a23beb16749e13e1d1de7c5be2c78dd6bcfcbb8168129bbd0ec2bacc21bf",
